If the corrected stochastic expansion and score bounds are available, the finite-dimensional triangular-array central limit step is elementary.  For a centered cell score \(\Psi_{g,h_n}\), the fourth-moment bound gives
\[
 \sum_{g\in\mathcal G}\sum_{i=1}^{n_g}
 \mathbb E_P\left\lVert
 \sqrt{\frac n{L_n}}\frac{\Psi_{g,h_n}(X_{g,i})}{n_g}
 \right\rVert^4
 \leq \frac{C}{n h_n^2L_n^2}=o(1).
\tag{12}
\]
Thus Lyapunov's condition holds uniformly.  The order-minus-two bias is negligible because \(\sqrt{n/L_n}h_n^{s-2}\to0\), and the desired mixed nonlinear remainder is negligible because \(\sqrt{n/L_n}q_{1,n}q_{0,n}\to0\).  The proved bandwidth calculation supplies both scale statements in its feasible window.  What is missing is the translation-aware expansion that identifies the summands in (12) and proves the required uniform score and remainder bounds.
